# 04 — Security (secrets · tenancy · RBAC · deps · docker · AI)

**Read `AGENTS.md` at the repo root FIRST.** It is the single AI entry point and
fixes the loading order: `AGENTS.md` → `memory/*.md` → `context/*.md` → `rules/**`
→ `skills/**` → `docs/**` → code → **then** edit. Never edit first and understand
later (AGENTS.md §0).

The authoritative enforced lists live in `apps/api/CLAUDE.md` (rules #1–#100, plus
"Security Architecture (Post-Audit)") and `apps/web/CLAUDE.md` ("Security Rules
(MANDATORY)"). Deep rationale: `docs/SECURITY.md` + `docs/security/` and
`memory/SECURITY_MEMORY.md`. Hard rules: `rules/security/`. When a security
invariant conflicts with a request, **the invariant wins — stop and surface it.**
These are AGENTS.md §6/§7 invariants: they hold in every environment, no `NODE_ENV`
exceptions (api CLAUDE.md #56).

## 1. Secrets — never committed, never fallback

- **Never commit secrets.** Only `*.example` env files, with **empty values** plus
  generation instructions in comments (api CLAUDE.md #53). gitleaks (`pnpm scan:secrets`)
  is a hard gate — a leaked secret fails CI (AGENTS.md §5).
- **No hardcoded or fallback secrets.** `JWT_SECRET`, `CONFIG_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, API
  keys, and `SEED_DEFAULT_PASSWORD` load from env with **no `??` default** — fail loudly
  at startup if missing (api CLAUDE.md #24, #54). All-zero / placeholder keys are
  plaintext: `env.validation.ts` `.refine()` rejects them (api CLAUDE.md #53).
- **Never log credentials.** The pino `redact` array (`app.module.ts`) covers
  `req.body.password`/`currentPassword`/`newPassword`/`confirmPassword`; the audit
  interceptor sanitizes `password, apiKey, token, secret, bearerToken, accessKey,
  clientSecret, refreshToken, accessToken, encryptedConfig, authorization` (api CLAUDE.md
  #57, #66). Frontend: never log tokens — not in `console.warn`, error handlers, or
  Zustand devtools; never store tokens/OSINT keys in `localStorage` (web CLAUDE.md §Security #39, #46, #55).
- **Connector credentials are AES-256-GCM encrypted at rest** via
  `apps/api/src/common/utils/encryption.utility.ts`. Validate connector config with the
  per-type Zod schema, then encrypt before storing (api CLAUDE.md #39, #96).

## 2. Tenant isolation — never cross tenants

- **Every tenant-owned query / `update` / `delete` is scoped by `tenantId`.** Never
  `update`/`delete` by `id` alone — always `where: { id, tenantId }` (api CLAUDE.md #8, #26).
- **Repository methods take `tenantId`.** Repos are pure data access; the tenant scope
  is a required parameter, not an afterthought.
- **Validate ownership before touching children.** Sub-resource endpoints verify the
  parent belongs to the caller's tenant before querying the child (api CLAUDE.md #75);
  linked alert IDs and case owners must belong to the same tenant (api CLAUDE.md #41, #42, #48).
- **GLOBAL_ADMIN tenant switch is server-only.** The auth guard overrides
  `request.user.tenantId` from the `X-Tenant-Id` header **only** for GLOBAL_ADMIN; non-admins
  cannot switch. Frontend sends it via the `useTenantStore` → Axios interceptor — never
  invent a tenant id client-side (web CLAUDE.md, api CLAUDE.md §Key Principles #8).

## 3. RBAC & auth — no bypass, ever

- **Every backend endpoint has `@RequirePermission(Permission.MODULE_ACTION)`** from
  `@/common/decorators/permission.decorator` (api CLAUDE.md #25). Permissions are
  DB-backed; GLOBAL_ADMIN always passes. Connector mutations additionally require
  `@Roles(UserRole.TENANT_ADMIN)` (api CLAUDE.md #55).
- **No auth bypass in any environment** — no dev shortcuts, no fake users, no skipping
  JWT verification, no `if (NODE_ENV === 'development') { skip }` (api CLAUDE.md #23, #56).
  Guard chain: `AuthGuard` (JWT verify + DB active-check + GLOBAL_ADMIN switch) →
  `TenantGuard` → `RolesGuard`. `validateUserActive` also checks active membership (api CLAUDE.md #31).
- **Role comes only from the validated JWT.** Never forward client-supplied `X-Role`/auth
  headers — not in the Next.js proxy, not in dev (api CLAUDE.md #76, web CLAUDE.md §Security #41).
- **JWT hygiene:** sign/verify with explicit `HS256`; every token carries `jti` +
  `tokenType`; verify `tokenType` on every check; logout + refresh blacklist old JTIs in
  Redis (api CLAUDE.md #29, #37, #38, #51). Auth/AI/mutation endpoints are rate-limited
  per the tier table (auth 5/min, CRUD 30/min, bulk 5/min, delete 10/min, AI 10/min — api
  CLAUDE.md #80).
- **Adding a permission is one end-to-end change** (backend enum + definitions + defaults +
  `@RequirePermission` + Prisma migration using `WHERE NOT EXISTS`, **never** `ON CONFLICT`
  (compound `(tenantId, key)`) + frontend enum mirror + Next proxy route + i18n in all 6
  locales + `prisma db seed`). See `skills/backend/add-permission.md`.

## 4. Input, SSRF & injection

- **SSRF-validate user URLs at input time.** Call `validateUrl()` from
  `ssrf.utility.ts` on connector + OSINT-source create/update (before encrypting), not
  only at fetch time — blocks stored `169.254.169.254` / internal targets (api CLAUDE.md #59, #95).
  Frontend OSINT forms validate via `isAllowedSourceUrl()` before save (web CLAUDE.md #54).
- **Bound every input.** Zod string fields need `.max()`, array fields need `.max()`,
  JSON/record fields need a `.refine()` ≤ 64KB; global body limit is 1MB (api CLAUDE.md #27, #28, #34, #78).
- **Sanitize Elasticsearch queries** via `sanitizeEsQueryString()` — strip
  `script/_search/_mapping/_cluster/_cat/_nodes`, `allow_leading_wildcard: false` (api CLAUDE.md #35, #79).
- **No injection sinks:** no `eval`/`new Function`/`setTimeout('code')`, no `javascript:`
  URLs, no non-literal `RegExp`, use `Buffer.alloc/from`, `node:` import prefix
  (`eslint-plugin-security` is on in both apps). Frontend: no `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`
  (`react/no-danger: error`); dynamic map access via `lookup()`/`.at()`, not `obj[var]`
  (web CLAUDE.md #21, #22, #36). Validate redirect targets against an allowlist (web CLAUDE.md §Security #37).
- **Errors never leak internals.** The GlobalExceptionFilter strips file paths, Prisma
  table/column names, and stack traces, truncates to 500 chars, in **every** env including
  dev (api CLAUDE.md #44, #63, #77, #82). Frontend shows only `t(getErrorKey(error))`,
  never raw backend text (web CLAUDE.md §Security #40).

## 5. Dependencies & supply chain

- **pnpm only, Node 22.** No npm/yarn lockfiles. Upgrade deps via
  `skills/devsecops/upgrade-dependency.md` — prove nothing breaks (`pnpm typecheck` +
  `pnpm build`) before merging.
- **Scan before claiming clean:** `pnpm audit:security`, `pnpm scan:trivy` (Trivy fs),
  `pnpm scan:secrets` (gitleaks). gitleaks + CodeQL are **hard gates**; `pnpm audit` /
  Trivy fs are advisory today (tracked debt) — run + annotate, don't silently skip
  (AGENTS.md §5, `rules/testing/quality-gates.md`).
- **Prove before removing a dependency** (or file/env var): check imports, routes, Docker,
  CI, Prisma, seed, tests, and `*.example` (AGENTS.md §8, `rules/global/branch-safety.md`).
- **No `eslint-disable` / `@ts-ignore` / `@ts-expect-error` / `any`** to silence a
  security rule — fix the root cause (api & web CLAUDE.md #1, #2).

## 6. Docker hardening

- **Production compose exposes only the API port.** Postgres (5432), Redis (6379), and
  pgAdmin (5050) get **no `ports:` binding** in prod — internal services talk over Docker
  networks only (api CLAUDE.md #65). Compose files live under `infra/docker/`.
- **No secrets baked into images or compose.** Secrets come from env at runtime
  (`pnpm setup:env` generates dev values); never hardcode them in Dockerfiles/compose.
- **No destructive Docker commands** (`docker compose down -v`) unless explicitly required
  and documented (AGENTS.md §8). Docker image builds are a hard gate — verify they pass.

## 7. AI security — analyze/suggest, never silently destroy

- **AI may analyze and suggest; it must not silently execute** destructive
  security/infra actions. Those are `approval-required` and need a persisted
  `ApprovalRequest` **before** execution, plus the permission (AGENTS.md §7, api CLAUDE.md #97).
- **Never render raw AI output as HTML.** Markdown via a safe renderer or plain text;
  `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` with AI content is banned. Transform inter-agent JSON to
  human-readable first (web CLAUDE.md #43, #58).
- **Redact before model calls.** Use `@auraspear/ai` `redact()` to strip PII/secrets;
  AI memory is tenant-scoped and stores **no secrets** (AGENTS.md §7). Never store AI
  transcripts in `localStorage` — server-side session only (web CLAUDE.md #46).
- **Provenance + bounds.** AI output carries provider/model/confidence and citations;
  AI endpoints are rate-limited (10/min) and token quota is checked before the provider
  call; every trigger evaluation is logged (api CLAUDE.md #33, #98, #99). Custom OSINT URLs
  pass SSRF validation and keys are encrypted at rest (api CLAUDE.md #95, #96).
- **No mock/fallback shortcuts in prod.** No `BEDROCK_MOCK` or env-gated mock mode; the
  connector cascade tries **all** configured connectors (bedrock → llm_apis →
  openclaw_gateway) before any rule-based fallback, which must be labeled `model: 'rule-based'`
  (api CLAUDE.md #88, #89, web CLAUDE.md #30). Validate agent/provider/trigger configs against
  their enums + per-mode Zod schemas (api CLAUDE.md #92–#94).

## Branch & proof discipline

- **Never work directly on `main`** — branch first (`feat/...`, `fix/...`, `chore/...`)
  (AGENTS.md §8).
- **`pnpm typecheck` (tsc) is the blocking typecheck;** `pnpm typecheck:fast` (tsgo) is
  advisory only — never cite it as proof. Don't say "all green" unless the required gates
  ran and passed; don't hide failures. The `qa-gatekeeper` subagent rejects claims without
  command output.

